[{"id":2744972773,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6jnPXl","state":"APPROVED","commit_id":"e1fcb85a44e7eb158c9d60340b3cea9a06b2b454","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?u=24618295fece29a0bf5c850faf2555985232f5f2&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","login":"aaronfranke","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke"},"body":"Indeed, that's much better. I consider the old behavior a bug.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105065#pullrequestreview-2744972773","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105065","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-04-05T19:34:24Z"},{"id":2744999459,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6jnV4j","state":"DISMISSED","commit_id":"e1fcb85a44e7eb158c9d60340b3cea9a06b2b454","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?u=34072b401722100a7c0c0d61e37b376cf22b4545&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","login":"Repiteo","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo"},"body":"It's a bit surprising that this *isn't* the default behavior for sorting `StringName`. Having to jump through the hoops for `StringLikeVariantOrder`, when that should probably just be the default. Obviously outside the scope of this PR, which just makes the sorting work as it intuitively should","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105065#pullrequestreview-2744999459","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105065","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2025-04-05T22:45:39Z"},{"id":2745095526,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6jntVm","state":"DISMISSED","commit_id":"e1fcb85a44e7eb158c9d60340b3cea9a06b2b454","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?u=8069d9b7bc6ab503ce83dfcfa53fd021672aeccf&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","login":"Mickeon","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon"},"body":"I must approve, given this is the expected outcome when I was writing the example. I can't help but wonder about performance drawbacks or potential side effects, but no one else does, so... hooray?","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105065#pullrequestreview-2745095526","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105065","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-04-06T10:00:47Z"},{"id":2745116113,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6jnyXR","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","commit_id":"e1fcb85a44e7eb158c9d60340b3cea9a06b2b454","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?u=24618295fece29a0bf5c850faf2555985232f5f2&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","login":"aaronfranke","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke"},"body":"Hang on, my approval was meant for Dictionary sorting. You can't do this to Array.\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nfunc _ready() -> void:\r\n\tvar arr = [10, 1.0]\r\n\tarr.sort()\r\n\tprint(arr)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis prints `[1.0, 10]` in master but `[10, 1.0]` with this PR.\r\n\r\nDictionary sorting is useful when you expect the output to be serialized to JSON or similar, so it makes sense to do it with Strings since JSON keys are only Strings. Otherwise, for Dictionaries, the order in memory in Godot does not matter and is considered an implementation detail. For Arrays, the order very much matters.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105065#pullrequestreview-2745116113","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105065","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-04-06T11:31:11Z"}]